ontrol group users have  two other control group members a triads  that include another protester again see  this very sad tale for protesters in a  very sharp decline for controls showing  that again protesters have significantly  more triads that include another  protesters  and controls do with another control and  finally also with a strong ties we again  see this log normal distribution with  significant difference significantly  more strong ties between protesters than  between control group members so all of  these tests we've done here are also a  robust to our choice of control set we  thought you know maybe our is just  something funny about our Paris control  that we chose we gathered another  control set of users who rather than  being Parisians are just French and geo  tweet from friends at some point we show  that this set is actually  indistinguishable from the parrot from  the Paris control set in all of these  tests that we have they have the same  ties with in-group triads in strong ties  etc further there's something on Twitter  calls verified accounts these are  typically different network hubs like  newspapers politicians famous people we  thought these might bias biases in some  way if if Barack Obama or Justin Bieber  follows one of the protesters this might  just seem like a dense denser network so  we remove all the verified accounts and  again we recapitulate all the results  then we ask ourselves well what if these  people that well tweeted from Placido  public are just a bunch of friends who  go places and tweet together from there  and they're not protestors at all to  answer that we just put up a box around  the plaza a public to see how often do  people actually tweet from there that  might not be protesters in over a period  of two weeks when we try that nobody  tweeted from there so it's not like a  twitter twitter user party gathering  place also we asked ourselves well what  if these people just don't care about  Charlie Hebdo or Paris users and that's  why they didn't go to the protest and  everything else is incidental but let me  remind you we collected these users from  selves users who had tweeted using some  Charlie Hebdo hashtags here is the  volume of tweets that mention Charlie  Hebdo or the associated hashtags for in  the blue line on top the protesters and  the green line in the middle  the  attenders the first spike right there is  the day of the attack and the second  spike is the day of the March and we see  that there are similar levels of  interest in this event both for the  controlled set Parisians we have as well  as the protesters so these are really  users people who live in Paris knew  about this cared about this tweeted  about this  by all accounts could have gone to the  protest chose not to so this is a very  meaningful control group to control to  compare to next one reviewer asked us  well how do you know these people didn't  just meet at the protest and form all of  these ties afterwards we did in fact  only gather all of these in network ties  after the after the protest had taken  place so using the Twitter API you can  know when someone started following  another user but when you get their  lists of followers its chronologically  ordered so you know who the first user  they started following is in through the  last lines so figure out if that's the  case then the protestor protester tides  would skew more towards the end of the  list this is not the case the normal  distribution both for protesters ties to  non protesters as well as protesters  ties among themselves some of you might  be French speakers and noticed that the  list of hashtags that are used earlier  to pick these users actually included  some some very negative hashtags such as  I am NOT Charlie or even I am Kawachi  where he was one of the shooters and  then we asked ourselves why did we even  keep those in there maybe we just got a  set of people who tweeted about this  using the negative hashtags and that's  why they didn't show up to the protest  so all of the negative hashtags are  actually big exists in both groups  strangely enough but in very low numbers  and most of most of these keywords are  just neutral or positive to the protest  and finally something I added just in  the last minute because topic models  seems to be a hot topic in this  conference so we did it slightly  differently here rather than topic  modeling texts I topic bottled  the follower lists of people so here I  imagine that the generative process  rather than me picking topics to write  my document about and then taking a word  from that distribution I pick a topic to  follow someone on Twitter from and then  I pick someone who belongs to that topic  so rather than topics being bags of  words topics or bags of popular Twitter  accounts typically these will be like  these are the football players you know  these are the left-wing politicians  these are comedians etcetera so you know  I did this for all of the people in all  three of our universities using all of  the most followed accounts in this big  matrix here sorry each row is one of the  users and each column is one of the  significant and robust topics that  emerge when you when you do this  analysis if you can see the the color  bar on the left side there has some  green red and blue lines indicating  whether this is a protester a Paris  person non protester or a france control  group non protester and the the pattern  that emerges here is that we have some  topics that are largely interesting for  Paris people whether they protest or not  we have some topics that are largely  interesting for France people whether  they're present or not but if you see  this dendogram on the right on the left  side signify as I try to cluster people  according to the people they follow on  Twitter without much greater success  than that so we can't really tell by  whom you follow if you'll go to the  protest but we do actually observe in 